course: dictionary
lesson: 10246
title: One word, two meanings: tomato
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tomato is a soft, round, juicy fruit, usually red. You can eat it raw in a salad or cook it in sauces and soups. Context tells you which meaning is used: «Ava's gran chats to her tomatoes every morning» is about plants growing in a garden, not food on a plate.
explain: Words can have more than one sense, depending on the subject. In science a tomato is a fruit, because it grows from a flower and holds seeds. In the kitchen we use it like a vegetable. The sentence and the subject tell you which sense the writer means.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Tomato sauce» means ketchup in the UK and Australia, «cherry tomato» names a small kind, and «tomato soup» is clearly soup. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A tomato is a soft, round, juicy fruit, usually red.
fact: A botanist calls a fruit the part of a plant that holds the seeds, so a tomato is a fruit.
fact: In 1893 the US Supreme Court still ruled that the tomato was a vegetable, for tax.
fact: Tomatoes turn red as they ripen, because they make a red colour called lycopene.
fact: Tomatoes first came from South America.
exercise: Ava's gran chats to her tomatoes every morning. What kind of tomato is she talking to? | A tin of tomato soup | A slice of pizza | *A plant growing in her garden | A bottle of ketchup
exercise: Why does a botanist call a tomato a fruit? | Because it is sweet like a cake | Because it is always eaten at breakfast | *Because it grows from a flower and holds seeds | Because it is round and blue
exercise: Which is the correct plural of tomato? | *tomatoes | tomatos | tomatoe | tomatas
test: In the UK, what does «tomato sauce» mean? | A red flower | Pizza | *Ketchup | Soup with bread
test: What gives a tomato its red colour as it ripens? | Blue dye | Sugar from a cake | Chlorophyll | *Lycopene
exam: In which sentence is tomato used like a vegetable in cooking? | The tomato grew from a small yellow flower | *Mum added chopped tomato to the soup | A botanist calls the tomato a fruit | Ava's gran talks to her tomatoes
